   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to amend the public authorities law, in relation to prescribing a\nuniform system of accounts for the power authority of the state of New York",
    "basePrintNo": "S1873",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S1873-2019",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Amd §1002, Pub Auth L",
    "lawSection": "Public Authorities Law",
    "memo": "\n \nBILL NUMBER: S1873\n\nSPONSOR: COMRIE\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend the public authorities law, in relation to prescribing a\nuniform system of accounts for the power authority of the state of New\nYork\n\n \nPURPOSE OR GENERAL IDEA OF BILL:\n\nTo require the Power Authority of the State of New York (NYPA) to\nconform their annual report and books of account with the ones submitted\nby electric and gas corporations to the Public Service Commission (PSC).\n\n \nSUMMARY OF SPECIFIC PROVISIONS:\n\nSection one amends section 1002 of the public authorities law by adding\na new subdivision which would require NYPA to file an annual report with\nthe Governor, the Comptroller and the fiscal committees of the Legisla-\nture, in exact likeness to the annual report which electric and gas\ncorporations submit to the PSC. This subdivision also requires NYPA to\nconform their books of account to the Uniform System of Accounts of the\nPSC.\n\nSection two provides the effective date.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nThe report that NYPA presently files with the Governor, the Comptroller\nand the fiscal committees of the Legislature is comparable to the annual\nreports that corporations send to their stockholders. These reports tend\nto be more flash than fact. The uniform system of accounts and the annu-\nal report, which this bill asks NYPA to submit to the Governor, the\nComptroller and the fiscal committees of the Legislature, is a thorough\ndisaggregation of a utility's financial condition with respect to all\nsales, personnel, plant and equipment. Such a report could shed much\nmore light on the Authority's operations than does the annual report\nwhich they are now required to submit.\n\n \nPRIOR LEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\n2018:A.9982Passed Assembly / S.8364 Reported and Committed to Rules\n\n2017:A.3773(Dinowitz)Passed Assembly\n\n2016:A.1975(Brennan)Committed to Corporations\n\n2015:A.1975(Brennan)Passed Assembly\n\n2014:A.8477(Brennan)Referred to Corporations.\n\n2013: A.4017 (Gabryszak) Passed Assembly\n\n2011-12: A.4250A (Gabryszak) Passed Assembly / S.5549 Referred to Energy\n\n2009-10: A.918 (DelMonte) Referred to Corporations.\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS FOR STATE AND LOCAL GOVERNMENTS:;\nNone.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nImmediately.\n",
